# Subagent guardrails (DEC-004 aligned)

**Do not rebuild Project Squad.** It remains archived under `agents/_archive/`; use current ephemeral domain roles.

## REQ-032 — Known failure modes (awareness only)

| Anti-pattern | Mitigation |
|--------------|------------|
| Role overlap | One owner per artifact; see Squad Brief |
| Scope creep | `Out of scope` block required in handoff |
| Vague DoD | Acceptance criteria in handoff before spawn |
| Contradictory prompts | Parent resolves; subagent does not reinterpret |

## REQ-033 — Boss never codes

Orchestrator (parent agent):

- **MUST** delegate substantial implementation to a currently registered domain subagent when delegation adds value
- **MAY** edit hub config/docs/rules when that IS the task
- **MUST NOT** write application code in the user's project while acting as orchestrator — spawn builder instead

Exception: trivial one-line fix when user explicitly asks parent only.

## REQ-034 — Structured handoff

Before `Task` spawn, fill `templates/squad-handoff.md` (mental or file):

- Objective (1 sentence)
- Context (paths, decisions, constraints)
- **Out of scope** (explicit)
- Acceptance criteria
- REQ IDs if from Notion registry

No floating context from chat alone.

## REQ-035 — Hierarchy

```
User → Parent (orchestrator)
         → current research / architecture role (plan)
         → current domain implementation role (execute)
         → current QA / review role (verify)
```

Max **2** agency personas per session (existing policy). Flat 9-agent fan-out **forbidden** without architect layer.

## REQ-036 — Verification gate

Parent **must not** mark DONE until:

1. Project checks or a current QA-equivalent review pass, OR
2. User explicitly waives verification

Failed QA → back to builder with handoff delta, not user.

## REQ-037 — Conflict resolution

| Conflict | Rule |
|----------|------|
| design vs build | Architect/spec wins; build implements spec |
| SEO vs speed | Document tradeoff; user only if product decision |
| security vs ship | security-review blocks ship |

## REQ-038 — memory

Record **why** (decision + rejected alternatives), not only **what**. Route durable memory through the parent and `user-memory`; never restore `squad-memory` automatically.

## Template

`templates/squad-handoff.md`
